WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.247
A strong reshape project includes validation.

00:00:05.247 --> 00:00:07.067
State the grain at every stage.

00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:12.157
Compare additive totals. Document the NULL policy.

00:00:12.157 --> 00:00:16.002
Confirm that expected categories and months are present.

00:00:16.002 --> 00:00:24.257
These checks make the transformation reproducible and reduce the chance of silent data loss.

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:32.377
Connect this idea to a survey project reshaping question responses for analysis.

00:00:32.377 --> 00:00:38.827
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:38.827 --> 00:00:49.772
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:49.772 --> 00:00:55.362
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:55.362 --> 00:01:03.440
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
